From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Maago <maago@example.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 01:23:58 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Keep the files in a bucket

media/ is a directory of one machine: a second copy of the server, or
a container moved to another host, does not see the files the first
kept. Since 0033 the binary keeps nothing but the database and the
attachments' media/; with a bucket, it is the database and the bucket.
Package contrib/s3 is a maago.MediaStore on any S3 API, AWS's, R2's or
MinIO's: main picks it when the environment names a bucket.

- BOARD_S3_BUCKET set: s3.Store, with each of its fields from the
  environment of the same name, BOARD_S3_ENDPOINT, BOARD_S3_REGION,
  BOARD_S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID and BOARD_S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY. Unset:
  maago.LocalMedia{Dir: "media"}, as before. The same store goes to
  Config.Media, to the worker's context and to the sweep
- main lists the store once as it starts, media.List(ctx, ""): an empty
  field stops the server with the field's name, as s3: Store.Endpoint
  is empty, and a wrong key or a bucket that is not there stops it too,
  here and not at the first upload. A bucket that is down keeps the
  server from starting, as a database that is down does
- A bucket is one site's, as its database is: the sweep deletes what no
  row of its own database keeps, so a staging copy pointed at
  production's bucket deletes production's files

The Dockerfile keeps the volume: with no bucket, the files are there.

diff --git a/main.go b/main.go
index 3619b3c..d3c5237 100644
--- a/main.go
+++ b/main.go
@@ -15,6 +15,7 @@ import (
 	"github.com/maago-web/maago"
 	"github.com/maago-web/maago/contrib/admin"
 	authlib "github.com/maago-web/maago/contrib/auth"
+	"github.com/maago-web/maago/contrib/s3"
 
 	"example.com/board/auth"
 	"example.com/board/board"
@@ -78,7 +79,25 @@ func main() {
 	// Where the files are kept, under names maago makes: a directory
 	// beside the binary, which the server does not serve as it is. The
 	// view that sends one down checks who asks.
-	media := maago.LocalMedia{Dir: "media"}
+	var media maago.MediaStore = maago.LocalMedia{Dir: "media"}
+	// A bucket instead, when BOARD_S3_BUCKET is set: a disk is one
+	// machine's, a bucket every copy of the server's. Any S3 API will do,
+	// R2's and MinIO's too. A bucket is one site's: never point a staging
+	// copy at production's, whose files its sweep would delete.
+	if bucket := os.Getenv("BOARD_S3_BUCKET"); bucket != "" {
+		media = s3.Store{
+			Endpoint:        os.Getenv("BOARD_S3_ENDPOINT"),
+			Region:          os.Getenv("BOARD_S3_REGION"),
+			Bucket:          bucket,
+			AccessKeyID:     os.Getenv("BOARD_S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID"),
+			SecretAccessKey: os.Getenv("BOARD_S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY"),
+		}
+	}
+	// An empty field, a wrong key or no such bucket stops the server here,
+	// by the field's name, not at the first file.
+	if _, err := media.List(ctx, ""); err != nil {
+		log.Fatal(err)
+	}
 	// The admin, at /app/admin/: the models of the apps it is given, to
 	// those auth.Can lets see them. The outbox's jobs too: one whose last
 	// attempt failed stays there, with its error.
